<title>ITALY: Italy's Naples sees March CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Naples sees March CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Naples said its March consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month on month and 2.8 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In February, Naples' inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 3.0 percent respectively. The general index and the housing and utility charges sector have been revised to take account of a court ruling that reversed electricity tariff reductions.</p>
<p>Naples is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Thursday and Friday. The city's CPI weighs 6.64 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes:</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to February 1997)</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.1    (0.2R)    2.8    (3.0R)</p>
<p>    Food				0.0    (0.0)     2.8    (3.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.1    (0.1)     2.1    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Housing/utility charges    -0.1    (0.1R)    2.5    (2.6R)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.2    (0.0)     1.7    (1.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.1    (0.2)     2.7    (2.6)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.1    (1.0)     4.7    (4.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture  -0.2    (0.3)     3.4    (4.0)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.4    (0.7)     4.3    (4.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	0.0    (0.6)     3.5    (3.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods and services    0.5    (0.0)     2.1    (1.8)</p>
<p>R - revised</p>
